# Generated MAP-017 schema evidence. These contain no rows or credentials, but
# they do describe the full authorization model (RLS predicates, grants, function
# signatures and search_path config) and should not be committed casually.
# scripts/map016-evidence/vercel-env-inventory.json is deliberately tracked: it
# holds variable NAMES only and is referenced as MAP-016 evidence.
live-schema-metadata.json
scripts/map017-evidence/*.json

.tools/map027-knowledge-pg-data/
.tools/map027-knowledge-pg.log
.tools/map028-channel-pg-data/
.tools/map028-channel-pg.log
# Agent scratch space: workbook build previews, generated artefacts, and one-off
# capture scripts. The delivery workbook's logic lives in src/lib/deliveryQuote.js
# and docs/specs/SHIPPING_AND_COURIER_LOGIC_SPEC.md, not in a binary here.
.tmp/
outputs/
.k2-shot.mjs

# Ambient-backdrop masters. The two source clips are ~3 MB each and only ever
# feed `node scripts/prepare-ambient-video.mjs`, whose ~430 KB output in
# public/ambient/ is what actually ships and IS committed. Keeping the masters
# out avoids putting 6 MB of binary into history permanently. If they should be
# versioned instead, delete these two lines — Git LFS is the better home for
# them if more clips follow.
assets/*.mp4
